374	     * it. A claim deferred on the sheet's today cannot be settled, nor one without proofs whose due is
375	     * above the proof threshold in force on its date (refused before the clerk limit is considered). A
376	     * SETTLED claim can only be voided by a steward, and only while the sheet's today is at most 7 days
377	     * after its settlement (its status log's SETTLED date); its frozen figure then leaves every total and
378	     * is recorded as reversed. A claim is given its number when it is settled (the next in the sequence it is
379	 * numbered in, by its due-by, unless it already has one), not when opened; a voided claim keeps its number, if it had one. An open of a claim whose due
380	 * is above the review threshold in force on its date leaves it in REVIEW instead, opened by the user but
381	 * until a steward reviews it (see {@link #review}); a REVIEW claim can only be voided
382	 * here. While the claim's person is flagged on the sheet's today, only a steward may open it. */
